Function tombstone (lg, main, sub) {
  // Check if the table is empty
  if (isEmptyTable()) {
    if (lg != null) {
      return sendError(lg);
    } else {
      return sendError(defaultLg);
    }
  }

  // Check if the last stored version is empty
  if (isEmptyVersion()) {
    return ErrRevisionNotFound;
  }

  // Store the tombstone
  storeTombstone(lg, main, sub);

  // Create a new version
  createNewVersion();

  // Decrement the keys gauge
  decrementKeysGauge();

  // Return Nil
  return Nil;
}

Function createIfCondition(condition, strict) {
  if (strict) {
    return `if (condition)`;
  } else {
    return `try { if (condition) } catch (err) { if (err === ReferenceError) { return false; } else { return err; } }`;
  }
}

Function: parse

Description: This function is used to parse the XML input string and return it as a Document object. If there is any error, it throws a SAXException.

Argument:
1. input: String, which is the XML string to be parsed.

Key logic:
1. DocumentBuilderFactory domfactory = DocumentBuilderFactory.newInstance(); 
2. DocumentBuilder dombuilder = domfactory.newDocumentBuilder(); 
3. StringReader rdr = new StringReader(input); 
4. InputSource src = new InputSource(rdr); 
5. Document doc = dombuilder.parse(src); 
6. doc.getDocumentElement().normalize(); 
7. rdr.close(); 
8. parseresponse(doc.getDocumentElement()); 
9. Agar koi error aajata hai to, wo humne SAXException throw kar rahe hain.

This code defines a function `add` which takes an argument `model`. The purpose of this function is to store all related model names in a `models_hash` named hash map. It stores the model names in different formats (e.g. without any special characters, '/' separated, and ':' separated). 

The only argument of `add` function is `model`, which is a model object. It collects all models related to `model` using `all_models_for(model)`. Then, for each model, it represents the model with three different names in `models_hash`: the original model name, the name separated by '/', and the name separated by ':'.
